 ## Overview
-The Tree Marcher is a hierarchical ray traversal algorithm that steps a ray through a sparse, hierarchical grid structure (such as an OpenVDB tree) to identify intersections with active nodes [S1, S2]. It differs from its siblings by operating directly on the tree topology using a Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) to skip empty space, rather than converting the grid to a mesh or tetrahedral volume [S1, S2]. It serves as the core traversal engine for [Hermite Data Computation via Bisection](822-hermite-data-computation-via-bisection.md) and [Tetrahedralization of Octree Cells](9049-tetrahedralization-of-octree-cells.md).
+The Tree Marcher is a hierarchical ray traversal algorithm that steps a ray through a generic adaptive grid structure (such as an OpenVDB tree) to identify intersections with active nodes [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of efficiently locating the first or subsequent node boundaries along a ray without visiting every leaf cell, leveraging the tree's hierarchy to skip empty or inactive subtrees. It differs from its siblings, [Hermite Data Computation via Bisection](822-hermite-data-computation-via-bisection.md) and [Tetrahedralization of Octree Cells](9049-tetrahedralization-of-octree-cells.md), by operating at the node-boundary level rather than computing dual vertices or tetrahedral intersections directly; it provides the geometric intervals ($t_0, t_1$) and node pointers required for subsequent isosurface extraction or volume sampling [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-The Tree Marcher uses a hierarchical DDA (HDDA) to traverse the tree. It does not compute voxel-level intersections directly; instead, it identifies which nodes in the hierarchy the ray intersects and provides the parametric interval $[t_0, t_1]$ of that intersection [S1, S2].
+The method implements a Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) specialized for hierarchical data structures. It relies on the parent's empty-space skipping logic to traverse only relevant parts of the tree [Parent](15494-octree-based-isosurface-and-geometry-extraction.md).
 
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** An accessor (`AccT`) providing access to the grid data, and a ray (`RayT`) defined in index space.
-*   **Output:** A pointer to the intersected node (`NodeT**`), and the intersection interval start (`t0`) and end (`t1`) in ray parameter space.
